  <section class="section scheme-dark" aria-labelledby="ai-title">
    <div class="container ai-def">
      <h2 class="h2" id="ai-title" data-split>Where AI helped</h2>
      <div class="text-lg prose" data-reveal>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>One source of truth, built by Claude Code.</strong> All 105 items live in a single markdown file. A Claude Code pipeline builds the whole interactive report from it, with count guards so no finding silently drops between the source and the report.</li>
          <li><strong>The plan rebuilds itself.</strong> Remove or regrade a finding in the source, rebuild, and the matrix and the Now, Next, Later plan re-sequence on their own.</li>
          <li><strong>Figma at every step.</strong> Each finding links to its node in the app's Figma file and in a separate audit Figma file, where the full IA map and flow inventory live.</li>
          <li><strong>Anonymised with checks.</strong> For this portfolio version, scripts rewrote every client detail and a leak scan blocks any client-identifying string from the build.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>The judgement in every finding is our designer's. The packaging is the system's. See how this works on every project: <a class="text-link" href="/ai-design/">how we design with AI</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

